lity":false,"_score_rev_volatility":6.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.030414575349671,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":62.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.001870149316880343,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.1254425621302526,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.0143198711244077,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":11.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06740195835645774,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":10.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.13116035810809218,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.023891856209408036,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":79.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0007022965095863473,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00601,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alaska Air Group, Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates airlines. It operates through three segments: Alaska Airlines, Hawaiian Airlines, and Regional. The company offers scheduled air transportation services on Boeing jet aircraft for passengers and cargo; and Horizon's and other third-party carriers scheduled air transportation services. It operates in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Costa Rica, Guatemala, Belize, the Bahamas, the South Pacific, Australia, New Zealand, and Asia. Alaska Air Group, Inc. was founded in 1932 and is based in Seattle, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Benito  Minicucci | President, CEO & Director and CEO of Alaska Airlines | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 31K people. Revenue per employee of $448K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $32K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $315 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Alaska Air Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.3B market cap on $14.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 12.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 13.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.0pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 91% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Alaska Air (ALK) a Buy as Wall Street Analysts Look Optimistic?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025396/is-alaska-air-alk-a-buy-as-wall-street-analysts-look-optimistic?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Caverage_broker_rating-3025396","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793971802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alaska Air Group (NYSE:ALK) Posts Earnings Results, Misses Estimates By $0.03 EPS","source