iation (1.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 39, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 95%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year, net $738K bought.","It returns 13.1% a year to shareholders (13.1% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 2.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 12.5% of the float, 3.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 31,787 employees, each generates about $448K of revenue, 1.2x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 9.1% a year.","That works out to $32K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":45,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (1.06).","pros":["Trades 91% below fair value of $422","Revenue grew 31.9%/yr over 5y","P/FCF 4.2x vs sector 22.3x","16 analysts' mean target $51.69 (+33%)","Insiders net buyers ($738K over 12 months)"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 25, gates 7/24)","ROIC 6.8% vs WACC 7.0%","Interest coverage only 1.1x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.06)","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)"],"flags":["Altman Z in the distress zone (1.06)","Operating income covers interest only 1.1x","The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":358.53,"vc":{"base":421.8,"base_src":"dcf","bear":169.39,"bull":1007.08,"alt_median":13.97,"n_alt":1,"gap":48.179,"dispersion":0.9601,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (96% dispersion)","DCF is 4818% above the other models' median ($13.97)","bull case is 5.9x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"ALK","date":"2026-11-06"}